# This repository is the code and data artifact for the paper. It carries the method, the scripts that
# produce every reported exhibit, and the result records those scripts wrote. Working material that a
# reader does not need in order to run, check or cite the work is kept out.

# --- Not part of the artifact ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# The paper source, its figures, proofs and correspondence. The manuscript is distributed through the
# journal; the Data availability statement promises the solver, scripts and results, which are here.
manuscript/
meetings/

# Working notes. Not part of the artifact.
LOG.md
CHANGES.md
TODO.md
CLAUDE.md
HANDOFF.md
.claude/

# Site-specific deployment state. reproduction/cluster/README.md documents what a site must supply.
reproduction/cluster/STATUS.md

# Superseded results and earlier pivots. Not safe to read beside current results.
archive/

# --- Excluded by size or licence ------------------------------------------------------------------
# 463 MB, not ours to redistribute, and holds a 197 MB file GitHub refuses outright. Fetched at a pinned
# commit by reproduction/tools/fetch_networks.py.
data/TransportationNetworks/

# Publisher copies obtained through institutional access.
manuscript/references/*.pdf

# --- Generated ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/
.venv/
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
*.before_*

# LaTeX intermediates.
*.log
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.out
*.spl
*.synctex.gz
*.toc

# Written by `make reproduce`: a demonstration that the pipeline runs, not a result.
results/smoke/
results/pilot/
# Machine-specific, not a result: reproduction/tools/record_provenance.py writes the reader's own.
results/provenance/
